Context
  /doc-align, then the user confirmed all findings were required.

Deviations
  One finding is deliberately NOT fixed here: gmake start still writes to the
  deprecated ~/.guile-skill root, so the README quick start documents the deprecated
  path. That is roadmap A6 and changes runtime behaviour rather than prose, so it
  wants its own change and its own consideration of where a contributor's transcripts
  should land.

  Six documented targets -- bench, calibrate, check-readme, scaffold, tail,
  test-project -- have no implementation. All six are proposals in docs/roadmap.org,
  written in the same 'gmake x' form as real targets, which is what made my own check
  flag them. Not a defect; worth knowing the check has that false positive.

Considerations
  The  guard is the interesting failure. It looked like the
  obvious twin of the bin/ guard and was wrong for a reason the bin/ one is not: bin/
  is dead everywhere, while CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR is alive in exactly the place the guard
  searched. Calibrating against the CLEAN tree, not just against a planted fault, is
  what caught it.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, as dsp-dr. gmake checks green; both guard directions calibrated.
